    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0157" n="129" xml:id="pg129"/>

                <head>68. Message to Athens<anchor n="1" xml:id="d68-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 70</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1956-02-02"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 2, 1956</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Since … meetings with Black and Nasr,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d68-f2"/> high dam
                    talks have taken turn for better with both sides giving ground. Have now agreed
                    exchange letters of commitment and Egyptians agree accept IBRD terms with
                    “appropriate” competitive bidding. Understanding include delay commencement
                    major work until Nile waters agreement. Both sides now optimistic. Black expects
                    remain until about 8 February.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
